<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Canton of Málaga</h1><p class="st-meta">1873 CE – 1873 CE · capital Málaga</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A federalist canton proclaimed in Málaga during the Cantonal Rebellion of 1873, one of the last in Andalusia to dissolve.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In July 1873 the federal republicans of Málaga, a city with a strong radical movement, declared it a sovereign canton, joining the wave of cantonal risings against the central government of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-first-republic">Spanish First Republic</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Local federalists ran the city through a cantonal committee and volunteer militias. The canton avoided open battle with the government and was torn by quarrels among its own factions over how far to break with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As the government regained control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a> after General Pavía's campaign against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-seville">Canton of Seville</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-cadiz">Canton of Cádiz</a>, the Málaga canton dissolved without a major fight in the late summer of 1873.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/canton-of-malaga.jpg" alt="Canton of Málaga" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bahnmarke_bleibt_an_Backbord_liegen.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1873 CE – 1873 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Málaga</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cantón de Málaga</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1873&amp;focus=canton-of-malaga" aria-label="Canton of Málaga on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4569 854 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Canton of Málaga lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4889 1110L4909 989"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4909 989h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4889 1110h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4889 1110h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Málaga. <a href="/atlas?year=1873&amp;focus=canton-of-malaga">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
